centage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9446,"playId":"401870766300","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9494,"playId":"401870766298","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9489,"playId":"401870766305","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9525,"playId":"401870766309","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9322,"playId":"401870766312","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.929,"playId":"401870766317","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.931,"playId":"401870766322","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.939,"playId":"401870766327","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.9393,"playId":"401870766333","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3992","guid":"68448bf8-769a-3082-81bc-dc47d2572605","fullName":"Williams Stadium (VA)","address":{"city":"Lynchburg","state":"VA","zipCode":"24502","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[]},"attendance":15335},"article":{"headline":"Deshawn Purdie, Ethan Vasko guide Liberty to a 35-3 romp over Sam Houston","description":"— Deshawn Purdie threw a touchdown pass before Ethan Vasko scored two of Liberty's four rushing touchdowns and the Flames spoiled Sam Houston's Conference USA opener with a 35-3 victory on Thursday night.","story":"LYNCHBURG, Va. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5138131/deshawn-purdie\" target=\"_new\">Deshawn Purdie</a> threw a touchdown pass before <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4832918/ethan-vasko\" target=\"_new\">Ethan Vasko</a> scored two of Liberty's four rushing touchdowns and the Flames spoiled Sam Houston's Conference USA opener with a 35-3 victory on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              Purdie completed 10 of 14 passes for 114 yards to help Liberty (5-1, 2-0) extend its winning streak to five. He added 57 yards on seven rushes as the Flames piled up 297 on the ground.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296294/jaylon-coleman\" target=\"_new\">Jaylon Coleman</a> led Liberty with 92 yards rushing on seven carries and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079364/kam-davis\" target=\"_new\">Kam Davis</a> added 67 yards and a touchdown on 10 rushes.\n\n\r\n              Purdie had a 15-yard scoring toss to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5215242/bryce-randolph\" target=\"_new\">Bryce Randolph</a> at the end of an eight-play, 75-yard drive and Liberty took a 7-0 lead on the game's opening possession.\n\n\r\n              Vasko ran it in from a yard out for a 14-0 advantage 45 seconds into the second quarter, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5154317/sam-carpenter\" target=\"_new\">Sam Carpenter</a> kicked a 36-yard field goal with 15 seconds left in the half for Sam Houston (1-4, 0-1).\n\n\r\n              Coleman and Purdie combined for 50 yards on back-to-back rushes before Vasko scored on a 3-yard run two plays later and Liberty took a 21-3 lead to start the third.\n\n\r\n              Davis had a 3-yard touchdown run on the first play of the fourth, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4880964/terron-kellman\" target=\"_new\">Terron Kellman</a> capped the scoring with a 9-yard run as the Flames improved to 26-1 in conference home games under Jeff Traylor — in his seventh season.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5148427/landyn-locke\" target=\"_new\">Landyn Locke</a> had 138 yards on 20-for-30 passing for the Bearkats, who turned the ball over on downs three times in the second half.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Sam Houston: Hosts Western Kentucky on Wednesday.\n\n\r\n              Liberty: At Kennesaw State on Oct. 22.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-10-09T02:28:26Z"}}